{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.WitnessObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.WitnessObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Monoidal.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.ZeroObjects"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WitnessObstruction.no_qou_on_moduleCat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WitnessObstruction.no_qou_on_moduleCat","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/WitnessObstruction.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**No module category carries a quantum observable universe.**\n\nThe composite of the two results above: `ModuleCat R` satisfies the\nhypothesis that kills the adjoint conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WitnessObstruction.moduleCat_unit_generates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WitnessObstruction.moduleCat_unit_generates","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/WitnessObstruction.lean#L67-L76","doc":"**In `ModuleCat R` the unit reflects zero objects.**  `Hom(R, W) ≅ W` via\nevaluation at `1`, so a subsingleton hom-set forces `W` to be zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WitnessObstruction.qou_needs_nongenerating_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WitnessObstruction.qou_needs_nongenerating_unit","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/WitnessObstruction.lean#L52-L65","doc":"**The two adjoint conditions are incompatible when the unit reflects zero\nobjects.**\n\nStated on bare data rather than on a `QuantumObservableUniverse` so that it\nis about the *shape* of the axioms and reusable: `hvanish` is the QOU\nobservability axiom, `hnontrivial` is `adjoint_nontrivial`, and `hgen` says\n`Hom(𝟙, −)` reflects zero objects. ","signatureChunk":0}]}